          "series_items": [
            {
              "activity_type": "patch_submitted",
              "subject": "[PATCH 1/3] kernfs: activate a new node without dropping kernfs_rwsem",
              "message_id": "20260913021453.21507-2-shakeel.butt@linux.dev",
              "url": "https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260913021453.21507-2-shakeel.butt@linux.dev/",
              "date": "2026-09-13T02:15:10Z",
              "in_reply_to": null,
              "ack_type": null,
              "is_ongoing": false,
              "submitted_date": null,
              "patch_version": 1,
              "series_patch_count": null,
              "version_history": [],
              "series_items": [],
              "patch_summary": "This patch optimizes the kernfs kernel file system by reducing the number of write locks taken on a root directory when creating new nodes. It achieves this by calling the kernfs_activate_one function before dropping the lock, which only activates the newly created node without walking its children. This reduces the overhead of acquiring and releasing the write lock for every new node, resulting in improved performance. The patch also includes statistics showing a significant reduction in write lock acquisitions after applying the change.",
              "analysis_source": "llm-chunked-no-replies",
              "review_comments": [],
              "list_id": "driver-core@lists.linux.dev"
            },
            {
              "activity_type": "patch_submitted",
              "subject": "[PATCH 2/3] kernfs: allocate the new name outside kernfs_rwsem",
              "message_id": "20260913021453.21507-3-shakeel.butt@linux.dev",
              "url": "https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260913021453.21507-3-shakeel.butt@linux.dev/",
              "date": "2026-09-13T02:15:20Z",
              "in_reply_to": null,
              "ack_type": null,
              "is_ongoing": false,
              "submitted_date": null,
              "patch_version": 1,
              "series_patch_count": null,
              "version_history": [],
              "series_items": [],
              "patch_summary": "This patch modifies the kernfs_rename_ns function to allocate a duplicate of the new name outside of the kernfs_rwsem write lock. This is done by creating a copy of the new name before taking the lock and freeing it again if the rename operation does not need it. The goal of this change is to prevent a rename operation from entering reclaim while other operations in the hierarchy are waiting behind it, which could lead to deadlocks.",
              "analysis_source": "llm-chunked-no-replies",
              "review_comments": [],
              "list_id": "driver-core@lists.linux.dev"
            },
            {
              "activity_type": "patch_submitted",
              "subject": "[PATCH 3/3] kernfs: free the old name outside kernfs_rwsem",
              "message_id": "20260913021453.21507-4-shakeel.butt@linux.dev",
              "url": "https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260913021453.21507-4-shakeel.butt@linux.dev/",
              "date": "2026-09-13T02:15:25Z",
              "in_reply_to": null,
              "ack_type": null,
              "is_ongoing": false,
              "submitted_date": null,
              "patch_version": 1,
              "series_patch_count": null,
              "version_history": [],
              "series_items": [],
              "patch_summary": "This patch moves the freeing of an old name in the kernfs_rename_ns function outside of the kernfs_rwsem write lock. The old name is already unpublished by the time it needs to be freed, so there's no need for it to happen under the lock. This change helps prevent potential deadlocks caused by holding the write lock while waiting out a grace period.",
              "analysis_source": "llm-chunked-no-replies",
              "review_comments": [],
              "list_id": "driver-core@lists.linux.dev"
            }
          ],
          "patch_summary": "This patch set reduces the amount of work done under the kernfs_rwsem write lock, which is held for a long time and blocks other operations. The changes include activating new nodes without dropping the lock, allocating memory outside the lock, and freeing old names after unlocking. This should improve performance by reducing the number of write locks acquired and allowing other tasks to proceed while waiting for the lock.",
          "analysis_source": "llm-chunked-no-replies",
          "review_comments": [],
          "list_id": "driver-core@lists.linux.dev"
        }
      ],
